    "factsheet": [
        {
            "heading": "The Evolution of Eye Care: Museum Tour",
            "paragraphs": [
                "Join us for a guided tour of The Royal College of Ophthalmologists’ museum collection at 18 Stephenson Way, exploring the development of eye care through more than 300 years of ophthalmic history.",
                "Visitors will be introduced to four displays from the College’s museum collection, featuring more than 200 historic artefacts. The tour will look at the evolution of cataract surgery, surgical equipment through the ages, teaching and testing methods used in ophthalmology, and some of the more unusual curiosities from the history of eye care.",
                "Alongside the museum displays, visitors will also have the opportunity to view parts of the College's building. Together, the tour offers a rare chance to see how the profession has evolved — from historic instruments and early techniques to contemporary education and training.",
                "The museum is not usually open for public access, with visits normally arranged by appointment, so this Open House Festival event offers a special opportunity to explore the College’s collection and learn more about the history and future of ophthalmology."
            ]
        }
    ],
